    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d465">

                <pb facs="0446" n="438" xml:id="pg438"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2531/606: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-21T13:00:00-04:00">December 21,
                            1939—l p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 12:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>239. Referring to my telegram No. 238 of December 20, 7 p.m.,<anchor n="41"
                        xml:id="d465-f1"/> conveying Chile’s consent to the publication of a
                    statement at Washington to the effect that the pending trade agreement will not
                    affect the copper tax in the United States,<anchor n="42" xml:id="d465-f2"/> it
                    is important to explain that Chile’s consent was based upon the telephone
                    communication received by the Embassy from the Department on the afternoon of
                    December 18 to the effect that Chile’s acceptance would result in very
                    sympathetic consideration by the Department to a revision of Schedules I and II
                    to render them more favorable to Chile.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
